      "year": 2023,
      "abstract": "ABSTRACT:The covid-19 pandemic provides the most recent example of the international normalization of the state of emergency. In this context, the present article explores the role of literature in responding to crisis when crisis is no longer understood as exceptional. Through a theoretical basis in Iser's The Reading Process', Benjamin's 'On the Concept of History', Adorno's Aspects of the New Right-Wing Extremism, and Derrida's 'Before the Law', the article undertakes a comparative reading of Saramago's Blindness and Charles Yu's 'Systems', arguing that stories themselves work as acts of protest, re-exceptionalizing crisis where it has otherwise been normalized.",
